 I can't take much more of this.

246
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:18,030
 Eyes off.

247
00:19:26,210 --> 00:19:28,290
 So, hapless denizens of this human body,

248
00:19:28,570 --> 00:19:29,910
 be you platelets or capustles,

249
00:19:30,050 --> 00:19:32,890
 we have come to rid you of the plague.

250
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:36,080
 These loathsome toxin flies who rule the roost,

251
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,060
 or so they think,

252
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:39,060
 will get a rude awakening from us chevaliers.

253
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:41,800
 Have at them a very palpable hit.

254
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:42,560
 Dead.

255
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:44,220
 For a ducat, I say.

256
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:44,990
 Dead.

257
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,910
 They've come just in time.

258
00:19:47,910 --> 00:19:49,790
 The toxins have got the upper hand.

259
00:19:52,110 --> 00:19:55,930
 We may have missed out on vaccination, but now, fortunately, we've got the next best thing.

260
00:19:56,090 --> 00:19:57,350
 Anti-Tetanus Serum.

261
00:19:57,730 --> 00:20:00,690
 Our doctor friend outside the body has very powerful weapons.

262
00:20:01,250 --> 00:20:04,010
 Look, Lieutenant, now the battle's really going to begin in earnest.

263
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:12,530
 Men!

264
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,520
 Those antibodies have really got it in for us, I'm telling you.

265
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,040
 Get angry with them, lads.

266
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:19,360
 Smash their faces in and do the worst you can.

267
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:21,460
 That's the only way we'll win, okay, okay?

268
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:22,940
 You mustn't fight, men!

269
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:29,150
 That's all we can do for him at present.

270
00:20:29,390 --> 00:20:31,910
 We'll just have to wait for the serum to take effect.

271
00:20:31,910 --> 00:20:33,320
 It shouldn't be very long.

272
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:37,650
 It'll kill the toxins while the antibiotic wipes out the germs.

273
00:20:48,430 --> 00:20:58,410
 When we get to the skin, that's where we're delivering our oxygen.

274
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:00,860
 Look at this.

275
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:04,650
 It's like antibiotic to me.

276
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:11,910
 We must be close to them now.

277
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:16,540
 Antibodies. There must be microbes about with all this military traffic.

278
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:23,770
 Going to be a war?

279
00:21:24,090 --> 00:21:25,720
 Oh yes, I should think so, child.

280
00:21:26,130 --> 00:21:30,420
 Those are the antibodies of an antibiotic, a medicine made to fight microbes.

281
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:33,480
 The war will go on until all the microbes are dead.

282
00:21:35,530 --> 00:21:39,300
 We're almost on them.

283
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:43,420
 The idea is to take them by surprise before they've had time to multiply.

284
00:21:44,230 --> 00:21:45,830
 Follow me, antibodies!

285
00:21:47,840 --> 00:22:16,480
 These two mosquitoes can't hurt a germ like me.

286
00:22:18,270 --> 00:22:20,780
 You can't bash me.

287
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:22,880
 Miss me. Try again.

288
00:22:23,590 --> 00:22:24,070
 Whoopsie.

289
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:25,730
 You have to do better than that.

290
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,840
 Over here. This way, you great ox.

291
00:22:30,730 --> 00:22:32,010
 Okay, chaps.

292
00:22:33,270 --> 00:22:35,430
 Punch her the spin bag. He's full of hot air.

293
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:48,830
 Lieutenant Claire of the Lymphocyte Patrol calling.

294
00:22:48,830 --> 00:22:51,050
 Please send in the macrophages to mop up.

295
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:53,890
 The tetanus infection has been completely eliminated.

296
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:54,850
 Over and out.

297
00:22:58,830 --> 00:23:03,440
 Swords, my gallant band of antibodies.

298
00:23:04,350 --> 00:23:05,950
 Tis time they should be blooded.

299
00:23:06,620 --> 00:23:07,600
 The choice awaits us.

300
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:08,580
 Death or glory.

301
00:23:08,940 --> 00:23:09,220
 Charge!

302
00:23:11,930 --> 00:23:16,250
 You fellows, give them everything you've got.

303
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:18,940
 Use your boots and teeth if you have to.

304
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:19,390
 Charge!

305
00:23:23,910 --> 00:23:27,030
 Porter, given or asked.

306
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:29,110
 Have at you.

307
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:29,900
 A hit.

308
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:31,900
 A very palpable hit.

309
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:32,460
 Ha ha.

310
00:23:33,340 --> 00:23:34,520
 Next, please.

311
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:40,000
 Oh, we'll wipe each other out this.

312
00:23:40,060 --> 00:23:40,320
 Stupid.

313
00:23:40,830 --> 00:23:42,720
 I'm going to puddle off.

314
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:45,540
 Look behind you, Metro.

315
00:23:45,780 --> 00:23:47,200
 One of them's trying to get away.

316
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:51,590
 We don't want him to become a new source of infection.

317
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:53,860
 Grab this and hold on tight.

318
00:23:56,700 --> 00:23:59,870
 To be...

319
00:23:59,870 --> 00:24:06,010
 B is the question.

320
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:10,190
 Well, my young friend, you've had a narrow escape, no mistake about it.

321
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:14,010
 Tetanus can kill you, no, but we were lucky to catch you at an early stage.

322
00:24:14,170 --> 00:24:15,520
 Everyone should be vaccinated.

323
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:18,490
 Doctor, vaccines for other diseases?

324
00:24:18,940 --> 00:24:21,690
 Good heavens, yes, there are dozens of them.

